For all $G = (\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E}, P_V)$, let $\Gamma(G)$ be the collection of independent sets of vertices in $G$. The K\"{o}rner graph entropy of $G$ is defined by
\begin{align}
    H_\kappa(G) = \min_{V \in W \in \Gamma(G)} I(W;V), \label{eq:wheee}
\end{align}
where the minimum is taken over all distributions $P_{W|V} \in \Delta(\mathcal{W})^{\mathcal{V}}$, with $\mathcal{W} = \Gamma(G)$ and with the constraint that the random vertex $V$ belongs to the random independent set $W$ with probability one, i.e. $V \in W \in \Gamma(G)$ in \eqref{eq:wheee}.

\begin{align}
    H_\kappa(G) = \min_{V \in W \in \Gamma(G)} I(W;V), \label{eq:wheee}
\end{align}

